"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114670","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114670","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114670.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114670.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This PR implements a solution to allow creation of custom upscalers. It's based on the same approach we've used for compositor effects, e.g once configured the rendering engine does a callback into the custom code to perform the actual upscaling.\r\n\r\nThe current approach only targets Forward+ and performs upscaling right after 3D rendering but before post processing similar to FSR2 and Temporal MetalFX. In theory you should be able to re-implement either using this approach.\r\n\r\nVery simple test project that does a 2x2 upscale:\r\nhttps://codeberg.org/BastiaanOlij/test-custom-upscaler\r\n\r\nOnly outstanding issue that I'm not sure how to solve is that I can't set project settings for this so the default viewport is setup with a custom upscaler. The main issue here is that we suppress MetalFX, so adding Custom as a enum at the end is not possible (unless there is an alternative way to fill the dropdown).\r\n\r\nImplements: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13718","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114670/reactions","total_count":24,"+1":22,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114670/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}